<clickhouse>
    <!--
        Per-node memory ceiling.

        By default a ClickHouse server assumes it is alone on the machine and
        allows itself roughly 90% of the host's RAM. Six servers each making that
        assumption on one host oversubscribe memory several times over, and the
        kernel then kills them (exit code 137). That is what caused the repeated
        restarts on this project.

        Each node is capped explicitly here. Six nodes at 1.1 GB total about
        6.6 GB, which is why this topology needs more than the 6 GB testing
        allocation and is gated behind `--profile full`.

        The budget this was originally written against reserved ~1 GB for Oracle.
        Oracle is gone: gold moved to PostgreSQL, which holds ~34 MB in the same
        role. That gigabyte is NOT spare, though — the processing container now
        runs Spark's driver JVM resident (`SPARK_MASTER=local[*]`), which is
        ~1.7 GB on its own and is the largest single consumer in the stack. See
        the memory table in the README.

        Raise these values if the Docker memory limit is raised.

        NOTE: only SERVER-level settings belong in this file. Per-query limits
        such as max_memory_usage are profile settings and live in users.xml;
        placing them here prevents the server from starting.
    -->
    <max_server_memory_usage>1100000000</max_server_memory_usage>

    <!-- Caches are per-node too, so keep them modest. -->
    <mark_cache_size>134217728</mark_cache_size>
    <uncompressed_cache_size>0</uncompressed_cache_size>
</clickhouse>
